<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fukuoka Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukuoka">Fukuoka</a> Prefecture is a prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, with its capital at Fukuoka. It was created in 1871 from the Fukuoka domain when the domains were abolished, and took its present form in 1876 by merging with the prefectures formed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokura">Kokura</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurume">Kurume</a> and Yanagawa. Long Japan's gateway to the Asian mainland, it includes the industrial city of Kitakyushu and was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> mining.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fukuoka-prefecture.jpg" alt="Fukuoka Prefecture" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nryate · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fukuoka_Skyline_of_Seaside_Momochi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
